<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nihil Novi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1505</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nihil Novi was a constitutional act adopted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1505, whose name means nothing new. It established that no new law could be enacted without the consent of the noble parliament, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a>. It was a foundation of the noble democracy and limited monarchy of the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p></div>
